      en: ["Spanning 2,613 square kilometers, it is the largest national park in Ukraine by area.", "The Tovtry hills are the world's only land-based remains of a Miocene barrier reef.", "Over 1,700 different vascular plant species have been scientifically recorded in the park.", "Approximately 60 plant species in the park are officially listed as endangered.", "The Dniester Canyon within the park is considered one of the Seven Natural Wonders of Ukraine.", "Rare species of protected bats inhabit the various limestone caves found throughout the park."],
